  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 225 PM EDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\n- Beautiful Fall Conditions through Tuesday\n\nHigh pressure remains in place with troughing to our east and\nwest. Mostly sunny conditions are expected through Tuesday with\nhighs in the upper 60s along the lakeshore to mid 70s further\ninland. Lows overnight will mainly be in the 40s with a few spots\npotentially dropping into the upper 30s tonight toward US-10.\n\n- Rain Chances Return Tuesday Night and Continue through Week\n\nCluster analysis and long range ensembles all point to high\npressure weakening over the area midweek with a trough moving\nthrough late Tuesday night into Wednesday. Instability is low\ntherefore not expecting thunderstorms at this time. Moisture\nincreases with precipitable water values around the 90th\npercentile (1.6 inches) shown in the mean of each cluster in the\ncluster analysis. There are some isolated members that approach 2\ninches (record precipitable water levels) as mentioned in the\nprevious discussion, however those probabilities are low.\n\nAdditional shortwaves move through the area for the remainder of\nnext week. There are some differences in the extended with the\ntiming of each of these shortwaves, but ensembles show agreement\nthat most will see some rain accumulations each day. WPC\nhighlights rainfall amounts in the 1-2 inch range Tuesday through\nSaturday. Some isolated higher amounts are possible (20 percent) \nas highlighted by individual ensemble members.",
